      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The arrondissement, also known as Hôtel-de-Ville, is situated on the right bank of the River Seine.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4th_arrondissement_of_Paris",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Since the 1990s, gay culture has influenced the arrondissement, with new residents opening a number of bars and cafés in the area by the town hall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4th_arrondissement_of_Paris",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 4th arrondissement is known for its little streets, cafés, and shops but is often regarded by Parisians as expensive and congested.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4th_arrondissement_of_Paris",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The 4th arrondissement contains the Renaissance-era Paris City Hall, rebuilt between 1874 and 1882.",
